{"kind":"propose","text":"PROPOSAL for hugh: adopt notes/2026-08-30-staleness-root-cause.md (artifact 051fcbf8 at exact head ec80e044 on request/staleness-root-cause) as the plan for fixing why finished and in-flight work sinks into the \"stale, not in flight\" population. ROOT CAUSE, verified against main 95c2b1e3: a merge-published artifact rests on the receipt, the receipt on the approval, the approval on the candidate's artifacts, and each candidate artifact on the artifact it replaced at its path; when a LATER merge at any of those paths retires that predecessor, the edge is artifact-to-artifact (never quieted), so the successor at an unrelated path goes stale — measured on the internal/app successor #14231, flared by four later merges at other paths (#14379, #14383, #14601, #14624). 154 of 332 live artifacts are stale and there is no fresh in-main artifact at internal/app, SKILL.md or internal/workroom. Downstream, the fold promotes the flag to a status (fold.go:3220, :3266-3268) hiding promised work; admission and reassignment refuse stale bases, forcing a refile loop with no exit; the merge closes only the exact approved head; and one request per review round orphans every earlier round. WHAT IS ADOPTED: P1 — a cause dated after a receipt does not flare the artifacts that receipt published, keeping the receipt-retired, condemned-succession and undated-cause flares; P2 — stale is a flag beside the lifecycle word, never a status, with the browser's duplicate 'stale' tab deleted; P3 — only retired bases are refused (fold half in flight as #13888) and the \"ask the author to refile\" discipline in AGENTS.md and SKILL.md is replaced by \"answer it like a fresh request and record the re-check in the artifact\"; P4 — no new closure rule: today's orphans are drained once by performer report plus requester ratification, and the drain-decision request #14687 is retired as answered; P5 — one implementation request per lane; a changes-requested verdict returns to step 3 on the same promise. P1, P2 and P3-fold land under one fold profile bump in the state@1 deploy order. WHAT IS NOT ADOPTED: the first draft's ancestor-head auto-closure and unchanged-path retirement, withdrawn on independent review as a closure-authority and path-authority hole. REVIEW: two passes by an independent Fable-model reviewer (not a workroom actor; findings applied in full, recorded in the note's frontmatter and commit message). If you want a durable second review from codex before ratifying, say so and planner files it. ON RATIFICATION planner files three implementation requests: (1) P2+P3-fold+P1 as one head with the profile bump; (2) P3-text+P5; (3) the one-time drain. Ratify to adopt, or record a dissent naming what to change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:051fcbf8a130baf81fd26ee28abcf465fd1db42f","head":"ec80e0448f8aa794e011430663421d08f86587ab","path":"notes/2026-08-30-staleness-root-cause.md","to":"hugh"}}